// Bun Snapshot v1, https://bun.sh/docs/test/snapshots

exports[`G2: thread status says what to do with each open request when the yield would be ⚠️ AC4: one entry per open request, the close command, --force only for old-shape question children, an open child listed instead 1`] = `
"**What to mark:**

- Request t-SESS.1 ("Find out why the export is slow") is in progress and nothing blocks it.
  - work done → \`br close t-SESS.1 --reason "…"\` (its open question for Justin stays open; questions never keep a request open)
  - not done, and you can go on → keep working; act on the default of any P1–P3 question Justin has not answered
  - not done, and it cannot move without Justin → file that question as a P0: \`bun run justin-sdk thread ask "…" --priority 0 --to t-SESS.1\` (already filed as t-SESS.2? File it again at P0, then close the old one: \`br close t-SESS.2 --reason "raised to P0 as <new id>"\`)

- Request t-SESS.3 ("Find out which change broke search") is in progress and nothing blocks it.
  - work done → \`br close t-SESS.3 --reason "…" --force\` (--force because its open question for Justin is a child bead of the request, the old way, and br will not close a parent with open children; --force closes the request and leaves the question open)
  - not done, and you can go on → keep working; act on the default of any P1–P3 question Justin has not answered
  - not done, and it cannot move without Justin → file that question as a P0: \`bun run justin-sdk thread ask "…" --priority 0 --to t-SESS.3\` (already filed as t-SESS.3.1? File it again at P0, then close the old one: \`br close t-SESS.3.1 --reason "raised to P0 as <new id>"\`)

- Request t-SESS.4 ("Write the export runbook") is in progress and nothing blocks it.
  - work done → 1 child bead is still open: t-SESS.4.1 — close it first
  - not done, and you can go on → keep working; act on the default of any P1–P3 question Justin has not answered
  - not done, and it cannot move without Justin → file that question as a P0: \`bun run justin-sdk thread ask "…" --priority 0 --to t-SESS.4\`

If you stop now the inbox will say: ⚠️ Open work, no blocker — Justin will be told to resume this session.
Before you stop, settle each open request: close it if its work is done; keep working if you can, acting on the default of any P1–P3 question Justin has not answered; or, if it cannot move without his answer, file that question as a P0.
Handing off is not a way to stop: run \`bun run justin-sdk thread handoff\` only when this session cannot go on (its context is nearly full, or Justin asked for a new session)."
`;
